    <section class="student-section">
        <h2>Step 0 · Prepare the application before the workflow</h2>
        <p>Set the prerequisites in <code>.env</code>. If you do not have resource IDs yet, the optional setup command creates the environment first, then a text-only agent, and saves each ID as soon as it exists.</p>
        <p class="student-source">Source: src/LessonC07.App/Lab/ResourceSetup.cs</p>
        <pre><code class="language-csharp">AnthropicClient client = new() { MaxRetries = 0 };

var environment = await client.Beta.Environments.Create(new EnvironmentCreateParams
{
    Name = "C07 student environment",
    Config = new BetaCloudConfigParams { Networking = new BetaLimitedNetworkParams() },
});
// Save immediately so a later agent failure does not lose the environment ID.
DotEnv.Save(envPath, "CLAUDE_MANAGED_ENVIRONMENT_ID", environment.ID);

var agent = await client.Beta.Agents.Create(new AgentCreateParams
{
    Name = "C07 text-only student agent",
    Model = new BetaManagedAgentsModelConfigParams { ID = "claude-opus-5-5" },
    System = "Answer the student's question clearly and briefly.",
    Tools = [], McpServers = [], Skills = [],
});
DotEnv.Save(envPath, "CLAUDE_MANAGED_AGENT_ID", agent.ID);</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="student-section">
        <h2>Sequence</h2>
        <div class="student-table">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>From → To</th><th>Message</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>1</td><td>Student → Browser</td><td>Enter a prompt and press <em>Start and observe</em>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>2</td><td>Browser → Blazor host</td><td>Click event over the interactive-server SignalR circuit (same origin, loopback only).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>3</td><td>Host → Anthropic API</td><td><code>client.Beta.Sessions.Create</code> with the configured agent, environment and budget.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>4</td><td>Host → Anthropic API</td><td>Open the event stream (<code>Events.StreamStreaming</code>) before sending anything.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>5</td><td>Host → Anthropic API</td><td><code>Events.Send</code> a <code>user.message</code> with the prompt.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>6</td><td>Anthropic API → Host</td><td>Live events: status running, model spans, <code>agent.message</code>, then idle, terminated or error.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>7</td><td>Host → Browser</td><td>Each event type, answer text, stop reason and the classified outcome re-render the page.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="student-section">
        <h2>Walk through the application step by step</h2>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3>1 · Create the session and open the stream first</h3>
            <p>The stream only delivers events that happen after it opens, so the host starts reading before it sends the prompt.</p>
            <p class="student-source">Source: src/LessonC07.App/Lab/SessionRunner.cs</p>
            <pre><code class="language-csharp">var session = await client.Beta.Sessions.Create(new SessionCreateParams
{
    Agent = settings.AgentId,
    EnvironmentID = settings.EnvironmentId,
    Budget = new BetaManagedAgentsBudgetLimit
    {
        MaxListCost = new BetaMonetaryAmount { Amount = "50", Currency = "USD" },
    },
}, ct);

await using var live = client.Beta.Sessions.Events
    .StreamStreaming(session.ID, new EventStreamParams(), ct)
    .GetAsyncEnumerator(ct);
var next = live.MoveNextAsync();

await client.Beta.Sessions.Events.Send(session.ID, new EventSendParams
{
    Events = [new BetaManagedAgentsUserMessageEventParams
    {
        Content = [new BetaManagedAgentsTextBlock { Text = prompt.Trim() }],
    }],
}, ct);</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3>2 · Apply the classifier to observed idle state</h3>
            <p>The handler reports both the stop reason and the classified outcome. A pause does not become completed merely because some answer text was received.</p>
            <pre><code class="language-csharp">if (ev.TryPickSessionStatusIdleEvent(out var idle))
{
    var reason = idle.StopReason.Json.GetProperty("type").GetString();
    outcome = OutcomeClassifier.Classify("idle", reason, false);
    await send(new("reason", reason ?? "unknown"));
    break;
}</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3>3 · Classify lifecycle and stop reason together</h3>
            <p>Terminated, incomplete, requires-action, budget pause and ordinary end_turn have different outcomes. The interrupted flag is an input to the classifier; the web path passes false and does not implement a cancellation workflow.</p>
            <p class="student-source">Source: src/LessonC07.App/Lab/OutcomeClassifier.cs</p>
            <pre><code class="language-csharp">public static string Classify(string status, string? reason, bool interrupted)
{
    if (status == "terminated") return Outcome.Terminated;
    if (status != "idle") return Outcome.Incomplete;
    if (reason == "requires_action") return Outcome.RequiresAction;
    if (reason == "budget_reached") return Outcome.PausedBudget;
    if (reason == "end_turn") return interrupted ? Outcome.Interrupted : Outcome.Completed;
    return Outcome.Error;
}</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="student-step">
            <h3>4 · Render the evidence in the browser</h3>
            <p>The <code>Home</code> component runs in interactive server mode. Each update is applied on the circuit and re-rendered, which replaces the Node app's NDJSON stream and browser-side parser.</p>
            <p class="student-source">Source: src/LessonC07.App/Components/Pages/Home.razor</p>
            <pre><code class="language-csharp">await Runner.RunAsync(text, update => InvokeAsync(() => { Apply(update); StateHasChanged(); }), disposed.Token);
if (!finished &amp;&amp; !failed &amp;&amp; !disposed.IsCancellationRequested)
{
    outcome = "Incomplete";
    status = "Stream ended without a terminal outcome.";
}</code></pre>
        </article>
